{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nNow I have a clear picture of all three bugs. Let me summarize and fix them:\n\n**Bug 1 (`merge.py`):** `_event_key` groups `tool_output` events by `(role, tool_name)` instead of using `event_id`, so distinct tools with the same name collide.\n\n**Bug 2 (`merge.py`):** Post-completion `debug_only` fragments are marked but never filtered out — they still get rendered.\n\n**Bug 3 (`incident_summary.py`):** Counts rendered lines (`\"rendered_lines\"`) instead of merged events (`\"merged_events\"`).\n\nLet me apply all fixes:\n\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /tmp/merge_patch.py << 'PYEOF'\ncontent = open(\\\"/workspace/replay/merge.py\\\").read()\n\n# Fix 1: _event_key should use event_id for tool_output\nold = '''def _event_key(event: dict) -> object:\n    if event.get(\\\"kind\\\") == \\\"tool_output\\\":\n        # BUG: tool outputs need stable event identity, not role/name grouping.\n        return (event.get(\\\"role\\\"), event.get(\\\"tool_name\\\"))\n    return event.get(\\\"event_id\\\") or f\\\"{event.get('kind')}:{event.get('sequence', 0)}\\\"'''\n\nnew = '''def _event_key(event: dict) -> object:\n    if event.get(\\\"kind\\\") == \\\"tool_output\\\":\n        return event.get(\\\"event_id\\\") or f\\\"{event.get('kind')}:{event.get('tool_name', '')}:{event.get('sequence', 0)}\\\"\n    return event.get(\\\"event_id\\\") or f\\\"{event.get('kind')}:{event.get('sequence', 0)}\\\"'''\n\ncontent = content.replace(old, new)\n\n# Fix 2: Remove debug-only fragments after completion instead of just marking\nold2 = '''        if seen_completion and event.get(\\\"debug_only\\\"):\n            # BUG: debug-only fragments after completion still survive as\n            # renderable tool blocks.\n            by_key[key][\\\"after_completion\\\"] = True'''\n\nnew2 = '''        if seen_completion and event.get(\\\"debug_only\\\"):\n            by_key.pop(key, None)\n            merged.pop(-1)'''\n\ncontent = content.replace(old2, new2)\n\nopen(\\\"/workspace/replay/merge.py\\\", \\\"w\\\").write(content)\nprint(\\\"merge.py patched\\\")\nPYEOF\npython3 /tmp/merge_patch.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
